[2026-11-03T20:33:11.141Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='packages/ui-devmode/src/foreign/adapter.js';s=open(p).read().replace('config = createConfig({ document: imported.tree, keyedProps:', '''const baseNodes = [...imported.nodeMap].map(([id, node]) => {\n      const properties = [];\n      const add = (label, value) => {\n        const original = originals.get(keyOf(id, label));\n        value = original?.value ?? value;\n        if (value === null || value === undefined) return;\n        const [name, key] = label.split(' ');\n        properties.push({ name, values: key ? [key, value] : [value] });\n      };\n      if (node.nodeType === 3 || (node.nodeType === 1 && \"'!node.children.length)) add('\"'text', node.textContent);\n      if (node.nodeType === 1) {\n        for (const attr of node.attributes) if (attr.name \"'!== '\"'style') add(\"'`attr ${attr.name}`, attr.value);\n        for (let i = 0; i < node.style.length; i++) {\n          const name = node.style.item(i); add(`style ${name}`, node.style.getPropertyValue(name));\n        }\n        for (const original of originals.values()) if (original.id === id && !properties.some((p) => p.name === original.name.split('\"' ')[0] && p.values[0] === original.name.split(' ')[1])) add(original.name, original.value);\n      }\n      return { id, kind: 'foreign-node', positional: [], properties, children: [], unknown: [] };\n    });\n    config = createConfig({ document: { roots: baseNodes }, keyedProps:''');s=s.replace('value = original?.value ?? value;', 'value = original ? original.value : value;');open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > packages/ui-devmode/src/foreign/index.d.ts <<'EOF'\nexport interface ForeignStorage {\n  getItem(key: string): Promise<string | null>;\n  setItem(key: string, value: string): Promise<unknown>;\n}\nexport interface ForeignController {\n  readonly host: HTMLElement;\n  readonly isOpen: boolean;\n  readonly storageError: string | null;\n  readonly restoreError: string | null;\n  readonly adapter: {\n    tree(): object;\n    nodeFor(id: string): Node | null;\n    idFor(node: Node): string | null;\n    applyProperty(id: string, name: string, value: string): { layer: string };\n    observe(callback: () => void): () => void;\n  };\n  open(): Promise<boolean>;\n  close(): void;\n  toggle(): Promise<boolean>;\n  select(id: string | null): string | null | undefined;\n  getSelection(): { id: string; type: string } | null;\n  setProperty(id: string, name: string, value: string): { layer: string };\n  exportOverrides(): { text: string; count: number; links: unknown[] };\n  exportSubtree(id?: string): string;\n  whenSaved(): Promise<void>;\n  destroy(): Promise<void>;\n}\nexport function mountForeignDevMode(options?: {\n  window?: Window;\n  storage?: ForeignStorage;\n  layout?: string;\n}): Promise<ForeignController>;\nEOF\ncat > .changeset/foreign-page-devmode.md <<'EOF'\n---\n'@link-foundation/ui-devmode': minor\n'@link-foundation/ui-convert': minor\n---\n\nInspect and edit foreign DOM pages with persistent LiNo overrides, subtree export,\na configurable bookmarklet and a private Manifest V3 extension. Allow DOM imports\nto exclude inspector hosts before assigning structural IDs.\nEOF\ncat >> packages/ui-devmode/README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Foreign pages: bookmarklet and extension\n\nDev mode also works on pages that do not use ui-dom. The foreign adapter uses\n\"'`importDom` from ui-convert, keeps node mappings in a WeakMap, and never adds\nmapping attributes to the page. The same inspector lives in a fixed shadow host.\nPick an element, open Properties, and edit leaf `text`, `attr <name>` or\n`style <property>` rows. Existing attributes and inline declarations are listed;\n`attr title` and `style color` are available even when absent. Arbitrary safe\nproperties can also be set with\n`linkUiForeignDevMode.setProperty(id, '\"'style background-color', '#eef')\"'`.\nEvent attributes, script URLs, `srcdoc`, and whole-style attribute writes are\nrefused. Text edits cannot replace an element'\"'s children. Closed shadow roots\nstay opaque; cross-origin iframe contents are not inspected.\n\nChanges write the session configuration layer and are automatically persisted\nper origin and pathname as LiNo under \"'`link-ui-devmode:<origin>:<pathname>`.\nReopening restores them; Save promotes the session to user and Discard removes\nsession edits. Reset restores the previous value, including an absent attribute.\nDOM changes re-import after 200 ms; stable IDs keep their selection. Structural\nIDs may change when siblings are inserted; use existing HTML IDs when possible.\nCopy overrides as LiNo exports one `set` per changed property; Copy subtree as\nLiNo exports the selected live subtree for migration. Clipboard denial presents\na selected textarea for manual copying. `whenSaved()` waits for pending writes;\n`storageError` and `restoreError` expose unavailable storage or invalid data.\n\nBuild with `npm run build --workspace @link-foundation/ui-devmode`. It writes\n`dist/foreign.js` (one ES module), `dist/devmode.js` (the extension bundle) and\n`dist/bookmarklet.txt`. Set `UI_DEVMODE_BUNDLE_URL=https://your-host/foreign.js`\nat build time to configure the bookmarklet loader. Host the ES module with a\nJavaScript content type and CORS permission for the inspected origin. The default\nURL reserves the future documentation hosting location; self-host the bundle\nuntil that location is deployed. Drag a bookmark whose URL is the contents of\n`bookmarklet.txt` into the bookmarks bar, then click it on the page to toggle.\n\n**Strict Content Security Policy (CSP) blocks the bookmarklet**, including the\nloader or its module request. Use the browser extension on these pages. The\n`tests/fixtures/foreign-csp.html` fixture checks this with `script-src '\"'none'\"'`.\nThe extension injects a packaged script in Chrome'\"'s isolated world and uses\n\"'`chrome.storage.local`; it does not fetch executable code from the web.\nSee [extension instructions](../ui-devmode-extension/README.md). Restricted\nbrowser pages cannot be inspected. No Firefox support is claimed.\n\nFor programmatic use, import `mountForeignDevMode` from\n`@link-foundation/ui-devmode/foreign`; pass an optional `window`, inspector\n`layout` LiNo, or async `{ getItem, setItem }` storage wrapper. The returned\ncontroller supports select, exportOverrides, exportSubtree, close/toggle and\nasync destroy. Repeated mounting toggles the existing controller.\nEOF\ncat > packages/ui-devmode-extension/README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Links UI dev mode extension\n\nPrivate workspace: not published to npm or a browser store. Run:\n\n\"'```bash\nnpm run build --workspace @link-foundation/ui-devmode-extension\n```\n\nRequires `zip` on PATH. The script builds the shared dev mode bundle, writes\n`dist/unpacked/{manifest.json,background.js,devmode.js}` and\n`dist/ui-devmode-extension.zip`. In Chromium, open `chrome://extensions`, enable\nDeveloper mode, click Load unpacked and choose `dist/unpacked`.\n\nVisit a regular HTML page and click the toolbar action (pin it if necessary).\nSelect a title, open Properties, edit text and style color. Reload the page and\nclick the action again: both changes return. The action toggles an open inspector.\nCopy overrides as LiNo and Copy subtree as LiNo provide the migration artifacts.\nChanges are saved in `chrome.storage.local`, isolated by origin and pathname.\nThe action grants `activeTab`; `scripting` injects the packaged `devmode.js` in\nan isolated world. `storage` saves the LiNo. No broad host permissions are used.\n\nUnlike the bookmarklet, extension script injection works under page script CSP,\nincluding `packages/ui-devmode/tests/fixtures/foreign-csp.html`. Internal browser\npages, extension store pages, and other restricted targets are unsupported.\nCross-origin iframe content and closed shadow roots are not traversed.\n\nThe automated `foreign.e2e.mjs` test loads this unpacked folder in a persistent\nChromium context, activates the actual action handler through its service worker,\nand verifies edits, storage, reload and strict CSP. This uses a test-only host\ngrant to simulate the activeTab grant Chrome supplies on a real toolbar click.\nTo verify manually, serve the repository, open the CSP fixture, click the toolbar\naction, edit the first title and reload/reopen. See PR #151 for the screenshot.\nEOF\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
