[2026-11-03T21:12:21.758Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_381","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat experiments/issue-58/plan.md; sed -n '1,200p' packages/ui-devmode/scripts/build-bookmarklet.mjs; sed -n '1,120p' packages/ui-devmode-extension/scripts/build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"# Issue 58 implementation and verification\n\nDependencies #25, #54 and related #55 are closed; no required sub-issues or comments.\n\n- [x] Foreign adapter: importer IDs, WeakMap reverse index, ignored inspector hosts,\n      safe text/attribute/style writes recorded in session, 200 ms DOM refresh,\n      stable selection, opaque shadow hosts.\n- [x] Async per-origin/path localStorage and extension storage persistence;\n      restore edits; LiNo overrides and selected subtree copy/export.\n- [x] Shared inspector adapter integration preserving ui-dom behavior;\n      bundled entry, toggle, fixed shadow host, configurable bookmarklet loader.\n- [x] Private MV3 extension: toolbar injection, activeTab/scripting/storage,\n      zip packaging and real unpacked Chromium verification under strict CSP.\n- [x] Unit regression coverage, fixture and browser acceptance tests,\n      accessibility and committed screenshot; README instructions and changesets.\n      Verification finishes with a whole-diff review and the four required gates on\n      exactly the committed revision that is pushed. CI results and the final acceptance\n      inventory are recorded in https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/pull/151 before\n      marking it ready; merging and deployment remain separate actions.\n\nLocal browser reproduction (reuse an installed Chromium with the optional\n`UI_DEVMODE_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE` environment variable):\n\n```bash\nnpm run build --workspace @link-foundation/ui-devmode-extension\nnpx playwright test packages/ui-devmode/e2e/foreign.e2e.mjs --config experiments/issue-58/playwright.config.mjs --workers=1\n```\n\n`UPDATE_DOCS_SCREENSHOTS=1` records the before/after and strict-CSP extension images.\nThe MV3 fixture uses a temporary host permission to simulate Chrome's real action\nactiveTab grant; the shipped manifest has no host permissions. The test dispatches\nthe actual registered background handler and injects the actual packaged file.\n\nThe real extension test reproduced ui-dom's null `customElements` crash (Bug #154).\n`packages/ui-dom/tests/kinds.test.js` reproduces the same environment without a\nbrowser; the null guard fixes it and preserves ordinary custom-element registration.\nimport { writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { Buffer } from 'node:buffer';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport { build } from 'vite';\n\nconst root = fileURLToPath(new globalThis.URL('..', import.meta.url));\nconst bundleUrl = new globalThis.URL(\n  process.env.UI_DEVMODE_BUNDLE_URL ??\n    'https://link-foundation.github.io/ui/devmode/foreign.js'\n);\nif (!['http:', 'https:'].includes(bundleUrl.protocol)) {\n  throw new Error('Bundle URL must use HTTP(S)');\n}\n// Inline the template: an injected bundle cannot fetch assets through the page CSP.\nconst plugins = [\n  {\n    name: 'browser-store-entry',\n    // The inspector needs the in-memory store, never the optional WASM backend.\n    enforce: 'pre',\n    resolveId(id) {\n      if (id === '@link-foundation/ui-store') {\n        return '\\0foreign-browser-store';\n      }\n    },\n    load(id) {\n      if (id === '\\0foreign-browser-store') {\n        return `export { createStore } from ${JSON.stringify(`${root}/../ui-store/src/store.js`)}; export { GENERATED_ID_PREFIX } from ${JSON.stringify(`${root}/../ui-store/src/ids.js`)};`;\n      }\n    },\n  },\n  {\n    name: 'inline-agent-template',\n    transform(code, id) {\n      if (id.endsWith('/agent-instruction.js')) {\n        const transformed = code\n          .replace(\n            /export async function loadAgentTemplate\\(\\) \\{[\\s\\S]*?\\n\\}/,\n            'export async function loadAgentTemplate() { return await Promise.resolve(template); }'\n          )\n          .replace('const template = await loadAgentTemplate();', '');\n        return `import template from './agent-instruction.txt?raw';\\n${transformed}`;\n      }\n      if (id.endsWith('/inspector.js')) {\n        const transformed = code.replace(\n          /export async function loadLayout\\(\\) \\{[\\s\\S]*?\\n\\}/,\n          'export async function loadLayout() { return await Promise.resolve(foreignLayout); }'\n        );\n        return `import foreignLayout from './inspector.lino?raw';\\n${transformed}`;\n      }\n    },\n  },\n];\nfor (const [format, fileName, emptyOutDir] of [\n  ['es', 'foreign.js', false],\n  ['iife', 'devmode.js', false],\n]) {\n  await build({\n    root,\n    configFile: false,\n    plugins,\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        '@link-foundation/ui-convert': `${root}/../ui-convert/src/html/import.js`,\n      },\n    },\n    build: {\n      emptyOutDir,\n      target: 'es2022',\n      minify: true,\n      lib: {\n        entry: `${root}/src/foreign/injected.js`,\n        formats: [format],\n        name: 'LinkUiForeign',\n        fileName: () => fileName,\n      },\n      rollupOptions: { output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\n    },\n  });\n}\n// Base64 keeps the configurable address out of JavaScript source syntax.\nconst address = Buffer.from(bundleUrl.href, 'utf8').toString('base64');\nconst loader = `javascript:(()=>{const s=document.createElement('script');s.type='module';s.src=atob('${address}')+'?load='+Date.now();s.onload=()=>s.remove();s.onerror=()=>{s.remove();alert('Dev mode could not load. A strict CSP may block bookmarklets; use the Links UI extension.');};document.documentElement.append(s)})()`;\nawait writeFile(`${root}/dist/bookmarklet.txt`, `${loader}\\n`);\nsed: can't read packages/ui-devmode-extension/scripts/build.mjs: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
