[2026-11-03T21:31:31.238Z] [STDOUT] {"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/58","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/58/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/58/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/58/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/issues/58","id":6146680339,"node_id":"I_kwDOVe76xM8AAAABbl7mEw","number":58,"title":"Development mode for pages not built with the framework","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12916356792,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVe76xM8AAAADAd_2uA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-01T12:07:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T12:18:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":22969357,"node_id":"IT_kwDOCoAzvc4BXnwN","name":"Feature","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","color":"blue","created_at":"2024-07-20T19:06:39Z","updated_at":"2024-10-08T23:47:30Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/75","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":2,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Context\n\nIssue #1 asks to \"modify the UI/UX on the fly on any of our websites\" (R9) and\nto make migration of existing projects easy (R23). Dev mode (#54) works on\npages rendered by `ui-dom`, where every element already has a `data-link-id`.\nMost of our sites are not built with the framework yet. This issue brings dev\nmode to them: import the live DOM into the UI dialect with the HTML/DOM\nimporter from #25, show it in the same inspector, apply edits to the\nforeign page, and export the edits as LiNo so they can drive a migration.\n\nTwo delivery channels:\n\n- **Bookmarklet**: a `javascript:` URL that injects a loader script. Zero\n  install, but a page's Content Security Policy (CSP) can block the injected\n  script.\n- **Browser extension** (Manifest V3): injects the same bundle with the\n  `scripting` API on user action. Code injected by an extension is not\n  subject to the page's CSP for script loading, so it works on more sites.\n\nThe deepcase application shell already shipped a Chrome extension target\n([deepcase research, section 1](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/main/docs/case-studies/issue-1/research/deepcase.md)).\nclick-to-component, LocatorJS and Onlook are prior art for \"select an element\non a running site\"\n([existing-solutions.md section 3](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/main/docs/case-studies/issue-1/research/existing-solutions.md)).\n\n## Goal\n\nA user on any web page clicks the bookmarklet or the extension button, the dev\nmode inspector opens over the page, shows the page as a LiNo element tree,\nlets the user change text, attributes and inline styles, and exports the\nchanges as an `overrides` document plus the imported LiNo of the selected\nsubtree.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- A foreign-page adapter in `@link-foundation/ui-devmode`\n  (`src/foreign/`): uses `importDom(root, options)` from #25 to build the\n  element tree and its `nodeMap` (link ID to DOM node), and implements the same\n  adapter interface that #54 uses for `ui-dom` pages: `tree()`,\n  `nodeFor(id)`, `idFor(node)`, `applyProperty(id, name, value)`,\n  `observe(callback)`.\n- Deterministic IDs from #25 (`id` attribute, else structural path). The\n  adapter never adds attributes to the page; it keeps mappings in a `WeakMap`.\n- Editable properties: text content of leaf elements, attributes (except\n  `on*`, `src`/`href` with `javascript:`), inline style declarations.\n  Applying writes to the DOM and records an override in the `session` layer.\n- Re-import on DOM changes (`MutationObserver`, debounced 200 ms), keeping the\n  selection when the ID is stable.\n- Persistence per origin: overrides saved under a key such as\n  `link-ui-devmode:<origin>:<pathname>` in `localStorage` (bookmarklet) or\n  `chrome.storage.local` (extension); re-applied when dev mode is opened again.\n- Export: the `overrides` document (with #55 if merged) and \"Copy subtree as\n  LiNo\" (the #25 output for the selected element), useful for migrations\n  (#65).\n- Bookmarklet: `packages/ui-devmode/dist/bookmarklet.txt` built from a tiny\n  loader that injects `<script type=\"module\" src=\"{bundleUrl}\">`; the bundle\n  URL is configurable at build time (default: the documentation site from\n  #62 when it exists).\n- Extension: `packages/ui-devmode-extension/` (private workspace, not\n  published to npm) with `manifest.json` (Manifest V3, permissions\n  `activeTab` and `scripting`, `storage`), a toolbar action that calls\n  `chrome.scripting.executeScript` with the bundled dev mode file, and a\n  packaging script that writes a zip.\n- The inspector is mounted in a shadow root inside a fixed host element so\n  the page's CSS does not change it and it does not change the page.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Publishing to the Chrome Web Store or Firefox Add-ons (needs accounts; a\n  follow-up).\n- Writing changes back to the foreign site's source code (Onlook-style).\n- Pages inside cross-origin iframes; closed shadow roots are skipped and shown\n  as a single opaque node.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- #54 (blocker): inspector, overlay, property grid, policy and the adapter\n  interface (if #54 did not define an explicit adapter interface, extract\n  it in this issue without changing behaviour for `ui-dom` pages).\n- #25 (blocker): `importDom(root, options)` returning\n  `{ text, tree, nodeMap, diagnostics }`, deterministic IDs and the security\n  rules (scripts and `on*` attributes dropped).\n- Related: #55 (export and share), #62 (hosting of the bookmarklet\n  bundle), #65 (migration playbook uses the subtree export), #13\n  (Playwright).\n\n## Step-by-step plan\n\n1. `src/foreign/adapter.js`:\n   `createForeignAdapter({ root = document.body, importDom, ignore })`\n   returns the adapter. `ignore` excludes the dev mode host element.\n2. `src/foreign/apply.js` (pure helpers plus DOM writes):\n   `applyProperty(node, name, value)` for `text`, `attr <name>`,\n   `style <property>`; refuses `on*` attributes and `javascript:` URLs.\n3. `src/foreign/persist.js`: `loadOverrides(storage, location)`,\n   `saveOverrides(storage, location, overrides)`, with `storage` either a\n   `localStorage` wrapper or a `chrome.storage.local` wrapper (both async).\n4. `src/foreign/entry.js`: the injected entry. If dev mode is already mounted\n   it toggles it; otherwise it creates the host element, imports the DOM,\n   mounts the inspector with the foreign adapter and re-applies saved\n   overrides.\n5. `scripts/build-bookmarklet.mjs`: bundles `entry.js` (Vite library mode,\n   ES module) and writes `dist/bookmarklet.txt` containing\n   `javascript:(()=>{...})()` that loads the bundle. Document the CSP\n   limitation in the README.\n6. `packages/ui-devmode-extension/`: `manifest.json`, `background.js`\n   (action click → `executeScript({ target: { tabId }, files: ['devmode.js'] })`),\n   `scripts/package.mjs` that copies the bundle and zips the folder.\n7. Fixture page `packages/ui-devmode/tests/fixtures/foreign.html`: plain HTML\n   with a nav, two cards, a form, an inline `style` and a strict CSP `meta`\n   variant `foreign-csp.html`.\n8. Tests: unit tests for apply and persist; Playwright tests that load the\n   fixture, inject the bundle with `page.addScriptTag`, select a card title,\n   change its text and colour, reload and re-open dev mode.\n\n## Files to create or change\n\n- `packages/ui-devmode/src/foreign/{adapter,apply,persist,entry}.js`\n- `packages/ui-devmode/scripts/build-bookmarklet.mjs`\n- `packages/ui-devmode/tests/foreign-{apply,persist}.test.js`\n- `packages/ui-devmode/tests/fixtures/{foreign,foreign-csp}.html`\n- `packages/ui-devmode-extension/{package.json,manifest.json,background.js,README.md}`\n- `packages/ui-devmode-extension/scripts/package.mjs`\n- `packages/ui-devmode/README.md` (bookmarklet and extension sections)\n- Browser test in the #13 location; `.changeset/*.md`\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] On `foreign.html` the Outline shows the imported tree with the same IDs\n      as `importDom` from #25 returns for that page.\n- [ ] Changing a card title text and `color` updates the page; reload and\n      re-open restores both from storage.\n- [ ] The page DOM has no attributes added by dev mode (Playwright compares\n      `outerHTML` of `body` without the host element before and after opening).\n- [ ] `applyProperty` refuses `onclick` and `javascript:` values (unit test).\n- [ ] The overrides export of the session parses as LiNo and contains one\n      `set` link per change.\n- [ ] `dist/bookmarklet.txt` is produced by `npm run build` in the package and\n      starts with `javascript:`.\n- [ ] The extension folder loads unpacked in Chromium in a Playwright test\n      (persistent context with `--load-extension`) or, if that is not possible\n      in CI, the manual steps and a screenshot are in the pull request.\n- [ ] The README states that the bookmarklet fails under strict CSP and the\n      extension should be used there (checked with `foreign-csp.html`).\n- [ ] `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, `npm run check:duplication`,\n      `npm test` pass.\n\n## How to verify\n\n```bash\nnode --test packages/ui-devmode/tests/foreign-*.test.js\nnpm run build --workspace @link-foundation/ui-devmode\nnpm test\nnpm run lint && npm run format:check && npm run check:duplication\n```\n\nThen run the Playwright test from the #13 infrastructure on\n`foreign.html` and attach a screenshot of the inspector over the plain page.\n\n## Prior art and libraries\n\n- click-to-component, LocatorJS (MIT, verify each): select an element on a\n  running page.\n- Onlook (Apache-2.0, verify): visual edits of a running app, writes code.\n- React DevTools and Vue DevTools extensions: content script plus panel.\n- Chrome extension docs: Manifest V3, `chrome.scripting.executeScript`,\n  `activeTab`. Firefox supports Manifest V3 too (check the current status of\n  the `scripting` API there before claiming support).\n- deepcase-app Chrome extension shell (see Context).\n- Vite library mode (MIT) for the bundle.\n\n## References\n\n- [ARCHITECTURE.md: dev mode](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)\n- [existing-solutions.md section 3](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/main/docs/case-studies/issue-1/research/existing-solutions.md)\n- [konard.github.io research (on-the-fly changes)](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/main/docs/case-studies/issue-1/research/konard-github-io-and-links-visuals.md)\n- [Chrome: chrome.scripting API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/scripting)\n- [MDN: Content Security Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CSP)\n\n## Conventions for every roadmap issue\n\nThis issue is part of the roadmap planned in #1. The full plan, the\nrequirement list and the research are in the\n[issue 1 case study](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/tree/main/docs/case-studies/issue-1),\nand the target design is in\n[`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n\n- **Read first:** `AGENTS.md`, `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`,\n  `docs/javascript-first.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n- **Links Notation first.** Every new format (documents, configuration,\n  tokens, styles, animations, recordings, asset records) is Links Notation\n  parsed with the official `links-notation` package (or the official port for\n  Swift and Kotlin). Never hand-write a LiNo parser with regular expressions.\n  JSON, CSS, JSX and so on are only import or export formats.\n- **JavaScript first.** Plain ES modules (`.js`/`.mjs`) with JSDoc types;\n  TypeScript declaration files (`.d.ts`) are allowed for public APIs. Swift and\n  Kotlin ports must pass the same shared fixtures as the JavaScript code.\n- **Tests:** `node --test` (see `package.json`). Every behaviour change has a\n  test that fails before the change. Keep tests deterministic: no network, no\n  real clock (inject time), no random seeds without a fixed value.\n- **Quality gates:** `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`,\n  `npm run check:duplication` and `npm test` must pass. Files stay under\n  1,500 lines (`scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`).\n- **Releases:** a change to a published package needs a changeset\n  (`npx changeset`), as described in `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n- **Licensing:** the repository is public domain (Unlicense). Our own assets\n  are CC0-1.0. A third-party dependency or asset must use a permissive licence\n  (MIT, ISC, BSD, Apache-2.0, CC0, CC-BY with attribution recorded) and be\n  recorded as described in the licensing issue. Do not add GPL, AGPL,\n  non-commercial or \"source available\" code or assets.\n- **Accessibility:** interactive UI follows the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices,\n  works with the keyboard, respects `prefers-reduced-motion` and\n  `prefers-color-scheme`, and meets WCAG 2.2 AA contrast.\n- **Scope discipline:** do only what this issue asks. If you find a defect or\n  a missing prerequisite, open a new issue (type Bug or Feature) and link it,\n  instead of widening this pull request.\n- **Done means:** every acceptance criterion is checked, CI is green, and the\n  pull request description says `Fixes #<this issue>` and shows how each\n  criterion was verified (command output or screenshots for UI).\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/58/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/58/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/pulls/151","id":5144045633,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVe76xM8AAAABMpvoQQ","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/pull/151","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/pull/151.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/pull/151.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/151","number":151,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(devmode): inspect foreign pages with a bookmarklet and MV3 extension","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #58\nFixes #154\n\n## Summary\n\nDev mode now inspects ordinary HTML pages through the existing inspector. The foreign adapter imports the live DOM with deterministic IDs, edits leaf text, safe attributes and inline styles, records session overrides, and refreshes after mutations without adding page attributes. Overrides persist per origin/path and can be copied as LiNo alongside the selected subtree.\n\nA configurable bookmarklet loads the ES bundle. A private Manifest V3 extension packages the same inspector for toolbar injection, including pages whose CSP blocks the bookmarklet. The inspector and overlay live inside a fixed shadow host. The shared adapter preserves ui-dom behavior; a null `customElements` guard fixes the crash reproduced in Chromium's extension isolated world (#154).\n\nBuild the bookmarklet with `npm run build --workspace @link-foundation/ui-devmode`; build the unpacked extension and zip with `npm run build --workspace @link-foundation/ui-devmode-extension`. Set `UI_DEVMODE_BUNDLE_URL` to a hosted bundle URL; the default reserves the documentation-site location described in #62. Hosting and store publication are outside this issue's scope.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Acceptance criterion | Evidence |\n| -------------------- | -------- |\n| Outline matches importer IDs | `foreign-adapter.test.js` compares the official importer tree and node mappings; `foreign.e2e.mjs` compares the rendered Outline IDs with the imported tree. |\n| Edit title and color; restore after reload | Browser tests select a card, edit text/color, reload, reopen, and verify both values through localStorage and real extension storage. |\n| No page attributes added | Browser test compares body `outerHTML` excluding the shadow host before/after opening. Reverse mappings use a WeakMap. |\n| Reject event attributes and executable URLs | `foreign-apply.test.js` rejects case variations of `on*`, control-character-obfuscated JavaScript URLs, unsafe style declarations and non-leaf text edits. |\n| Parseable overrides, one set per change | Browser test parses the exported document with the official LiNo reader and verifies two set links. Adapter tests cover restoring safe keyed overrides, clearing edits and replaced nodes. |\n| Bookmarklet build | Package build emits `dist/bookmarklet.txt`, ES and IIFE bundles; browser test checks the `javascript:` prefix and loads the emitted ES bundle. |\n| Unpacked extension loads in Chromium | Persistent-context browser test loads the packaged MV3 extension, calls its actual toolbar handler, injects the bundled file into the isolated world, and verifies edit/save/reload/toggle on the strict-CSP fixture. A temporary test-only host permission simulates Chrome's user-action activeTab grant; the shipped manifest has only activeTab, scripting and storage permissions. |\n| CSP limitation documented and checked | README documents CSP and unpacked installation. Browser test observes the blocked module load on `foreign-csp.html`; the real extension test succeeds there (screenshot below). |\n| Mutation refresh and stable selection | Browser test adds/removes nodes, waits for the debounced re-import, retains a stable selected ID and clears a removed selection. Unit tests verify opaque closed-shadow hosts and importer exclusion. |\n| Shared inspector preserves ui-dom behavior | Native inspector interaction tests exercise toggle, picking, Outline, property edits, reload/reset, policy and accessibility. `ui-dom/tests/kinds.test.js` reproduces the null customElements failure and verifies rendering after the fix. |\n| Required quality gates | Validation results and CI checks are recorded below. |\n\nReproduce the issue with the plain fixture `packages/ui-devmode/tests/fixtures/foreign.html`: open the built inspector, select the first card title, edit its text and color, then reload and reopen. Automated browser coverage is `packages/ui-devmode/e2e/foreign.e2e.mjs`; a bounded Chromium reproduction config is in `experiments/issue-58/playwright.config.mjs`.\n\nBefore opening:\n\n![Plain HTML fixture before opening dev mode](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/issue-58-547eaf00c7c9/docs/screenshots/ui-devmode-foreign-before.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter editing through the inspector:\n\n![Foreign page inspector with edited text and color](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/issue-58-547eaf00c7c9/docs/screenshots/ui-devmode-foreign.png?raw=true)\n\nReal unpacked extension on the strict-CSP page:\n\n![MV3 extension running on the strict-CSP fixture](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/blob/issue-58-547eaf00c7c9/docs/screenshots/ui-devmode-extension-csp.png?raw=true)\n\n## Validation\n\nOn `54e8a86`, after merging the latest `main`, all required local checks passed:\n\n- `taskset -c 0 npm test`: 3,606 tests passed, no failures or skips. One CPU keeps local resource use bounded.\n- `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, and `npm run check:duplication`: passed (2.90% duplicated lines).\n- `npm run check:assets`: passed.\n- Final Chromium foreign-page suite: all 3 tests passed, including the real MV3 extension on strict CSP. The earlier native inspector and foreign suite passed all 11 interaction/accessibility tests.\n- The packaging regression experiment builds with an empty `PATH`; independent `unzip -t` verifies all three packaged files.\n\nThe [complete Playwright CI run](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/actions/runs/41720220226) passed: 344 passed, 14 platform skips and 2 unrelated WebKit tests passed on retry (editor draft restoration and network initialization). All foreign-page tests passed on their first attempt in Chromium and WebKit; the MV3 test runs in Chromium. Native-web keyboard/accessibility checks also passed (2 tests). All CI workflows passed on this exact revision, including [quality gates and Node/Bun/Deno across Linux, macOS and Windows](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/actions/runs/41720220088), [CodeQL and dependency audits](https://github.com/link-foundation/ui/actions/runs/41720220149), licensing, workflow validation, link checks and example builds. The branch includes current `main`; the working tree is clean.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Every implementation criterion is covered by the evidence above.\n- [x] CI is green: `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check` and `npm run check:duplication` pass.\n- [x] Changeset covers ui-devmode (minor), ui-convert (minor), and ui-dom (patch).\n- [x] UI screenshots are attached and the complete CI Playwright suite passes.\n- [x] New build dependencies are permissively licensed; Vite 7 avoids Vite 8's MPL CSS compiler. Screenshots are repository-generated.\n- [x] Changes stay within scope; the prerequisite isolated-world crash is tracked in #154 and fixed here.\n","created_at":"2026-11-03T20:28:46Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T21:31:25Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5d8d8d1b142dfbb9477bb3eafc2890c1591adc9c","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/pulls/151/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/pulls/151/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/issues/151/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/ui/statuses/54e8a86f70d5a5a5a4e468b43c67a8c04b0322f2","head":{"label":"link-foundation:issue-58-547eaf00c7c9","ref":"issue-58-547eaf00c7c9","sha":"54e8a86f70d5a5a5a4e468b43c67a8c04b0322f2","user":{"login":"link-foundation","id":176174013,"node_id":"O_kgDOCoAzvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176174013?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-founda